---
// Version anglaise de /sms-conditions/ (conditions du service SMS, A2P 10DLC). Traduction fidèle.
// La version française prévaut en cas de divergence (mention en haut de page).
// Note : baseline, pas un avis juridique.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const siteUrl = Astro.site?.href.replace(/\/$/, '') ?? 'https://fournia.net';
const canonical = `${siteUrl}/en/sms-terms/`;
const maj = 'July 4, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="SMS service terms | FournIA"
  description="Terms of FournIA's text messaging (SMS) service: consent, message frequency, unsubscribing and charges."
  canonical={canonical}
  lang="en"
>
  <main>
    <article class="post">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">
        <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> <span>/</span> SMS terms</nav>
        <h1>Text messaging (SMS) service terms</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {maj}</p>
        <p class="traduction">This is a translation. In case of discrepancy, the <a href="/sms-conditions/" hreflang="fr-CA" lang="fr">French version</a> prevails.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            These terms govern the text messaging (SMS) service offered by FournIA (Simon Fournier,
            a business registered in Quebec, NEQ 2282026550), including the reminders and follow-ups
            that FournIA sends on behalf of its clients (for example an advisor) to their own clients.
          </p>

          <h2>Program and purpose</h2>
          <p>
            The messages are follow-up reminders and service notices (for example: investment
            follow-up, insurance review) sent to existing clients. They are not promotional or
            marketing messages.
          </p>

          <h2>Consent (opt-in)</h2>
          <p>
            Consent is collected <strong>verbally</strong>. When a client engages the services of
            their advisor (for example Karyann Turcotte, financial security advisor), or during a
            follow-up meeting or call, the advisor asks permission to send follow-up reminders by text
            message to the client's cell phone number, and tells them they can unsubscribe at any time
            by replying STOP.
          </p>
          <p>
            Wording used (in French): « Est-ce que je peux t'envoyer tes rappels de suivi par texto?
            Tu peux te désabonner en tout temps en répondant STOP. » (In English: "Can I send you your
            follow-up reminders by text? You can unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP.") The
            client agrees out loud, and the advisor records the name, cell phone number, consent and
            date in the client's file. This is not a sign-up through a website or a keyword. No
            purchase or account creation depends on this consent.
          </p>

          <h2>Frequency and charges</h2>
          <p>
            Message frequency varies: usually a few messages per year (follow-up reminders and one follow-up message), depending on your file. <strong>Message and data rates may
            apply</strong> depending on your mobile plan.
          </p>

          <h2>Unsubscribing and help</h2>
          <p>
            Reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to stop receiving messages. Reply
            <strong>AIDE</strong> (French for "help") for assistance, or write to us at
            <a href="mailto:s.fournier@fournia.net">s.fournier@fournia.net</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell or share your mobile phone numbers or your SMS opt-in data with third
            parties for marketing purposes. Details are in our
            <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. Messages are delivered through our provider
            Twilio (United States).
          </p>

          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            FournIA, Simon Fournier<br />
            <a href="mailto:s.fournier@fournia.net">s.fournier@fournia.net</a><br />
            <a href="tel:+15148632973">514 863 2973</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  main { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .post { padding: 8.5rem 0 4rem; }
  .wrap-narrow { width: min(760px, 92vw); margin: 0 auto; }
  .crumbs { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--mute-d); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--lime); }
  .crumbs span { margin: 0 .4rem; }
  .post h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.1rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.02em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--mute-d); font-size: .92rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .prose { color: var(--mute); font-size: 1.06rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .prose :global(h2) { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; color: var(--white); font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 2.4rem 0 .9rem; }
  .prose :global(p) { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .prose :global(ul) { margin: 0 0 1.2rem 1.3rem; }
  .prose :global(li) { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .prose :global(a) { color: var(--lime); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; text-decoration-color: rgba(183,217,76,.4); }
  .prose :global(a:hover) { text-decoration-color: var(--lime); }
  .prose :global(strong) { color: var(--white); font-weight: 600; }
  .traduction { color: var(--mute-d); font-size: .9rem; font-style: italic; margin: -1.2rem 0 2rem; }
  .traduction a { color: var(--lime); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
